        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    stock_returns = [4, -2, 3, 5, -1]\n    market_returns = [3, -1, 4, 2, 0]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    stock_mean = sum(stock_returns) / len(stock_returns)\n    market_mean = sum(market_returns) / len(market_returns)\n\n    covariance = sum(\n        (stock - stock_mean) * (market - market_mean)\n        for stock, market in zip(stock_returns, market_returns)\n    )\n    market_variance = sum(\n        (market - market_mean) ** 2 for market in market_returns\n    )\n\n    answer = round(covariance / market_variance, 2)\n\n    # return answer\n    return answer\n```",
